Package: mica-system
Version: 13.8+deb13u7-mica1
Source-Date-Epoch: 1790638915
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Mica OS <hi@micaos.dev>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: dbus, passwd, e2fsprogs
Description: Mica OS board-independent system policy
 The system half of every Mica OS root, and of the floor, whatever its init:
 the DATA layout, the seed and reconcile tools under
 /usr/lib/mica, the health gate and the boot-failure handler, the offline
 provisioning import, the mountpoints of /mica, /srv, /home, /root and
 /var/lib/mica, and the /var the tmpfiles entries describe.
 .
 It runs under neither init by itself: a product installs mica-systemd or
 mica-openrc, which wire these tools into its boot and provide
 /usr/lib/mica/mica-init, the one command the tools ask the init system
 through. micad is reached on the system bus with dbus-send. DATA's project
 quotas are mica-deploy's: its runkit sets them when it mounts DATA.
 .
 SSH and the console are options, not part of this package: mica-ssh carries
 dropbear, and a getty starts only once the console option has installed
 /usr/bin/login.
 .
 /etc/shadow is built in RAM at every boot from the image's factory copy, every
 account locked; a transient root password set through micad lasts until the
 next boot.
 .
 The postinst creates the operator account mica, uid and gid 1000, home
 /home/mica on DATA, shell /bin/sh, with no supplementary groups and no
 password.
 .
 passwd provides the tools the postinst runs. The verity root needs no
 userspace: the kernel assembles it from the dm-mod.create= table on its
 command line.
